<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>If we start with the initial condition <m>x_0 = 1</m>, use the graph to approximate <m>x_1=f(x_0)</m>.</p>

<graph xmin="-5" xmax="5" ymin="-10" ymax="10" size="large" aspectRatio="2" showNavigation="false">

  <function name="func1" fixed="true" applyStyleToLabel="true">x^3 - 8x
    <label><m>f(x_n)</m></label>
  </function>
  <line fixed="true" stylenumber="2" applyStyleToLabel="true">y=x
    <label><m>x_{n+1} = x_n</m></label>
  </line>

  <collect componentType="point" from="$g1" />

  <point stylenumber="4" name="p1" x="0.7" y="6.1">
    <label><m>(x_0, x_1) = ( <math displaydecimals="2" extend="$p1.x" /> , <math displaydecimals="2" extend="$p1.y" />)</m></label>
    
      <attractTo>$func1</attractTo>
      <attractTo><point hide="true">(1,-7)</point></attractTo>
    
  </point>

  <point stylenumber="5" fixed="true" x="$p1.x" y="0">
    <label><m>x_0 = <math displayDecimals="2" extend="$p1.x" /></m></label>
  </point>

  <point stylenumber="5" fixed="true" x="0" y="$p1.y" labelPosition="upperLeft">
    <label><m>x_1 = <math displayDecimals="2" extend="$p1.y" /></m></label>
  </point>
  
  
  <lineSegment stylenumber="4" fixed="true" endPoints="$p1 (0, $p1.y )" />
  <lineSegment stylenumber="4" fixed="true" endPoints="$p1 ( $p1.x, 0)" />

</graph>

<p>Move the <text extend="$p1.styleDescriptionWithNoun" /> to estimate the value of <m>x_1 = f(x_0)</m> when <m>x_0=1</m>.
<answer><award><when>
$p1 = (1,-7)
</when></award>
</answer>
  </p>
  
<p>
<m>x_1=</m> 
<answer>
<award>$x1ex2</award>
</answer>
</p>

<p>Check the accuracy of your estimate by calculating <m>f(x_0)</m> from the analytic expression for <m>f</m>.</p>
</exercise>



<solution>


<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
The following graph shows the equilibria as well as the point from the last part.

<graph xmin="-5" xmax="5" ymin="-10" ymax="10" size="large" aspectRatio="2" showNavigation="false">
   <xLabel><m>x_n</m></xLabel>
  <yLabel><m>x_{n+1}</m></yLabel>

<function fixed="true" applyStyleToLabel="true">x^3 - 8x
  <label><m>f(x_n)</m></label>
</function>
<line fixed="true" stylenumber="2" applyStyleToLabel="true">y=x
  <label><m>x_{n+1} = x_n</m></label>
</line>

<point stylenumber="2" fixed="true">(-3,-3)
  <label><m>(-3,-3)</m></label>
</point>
<point stylenumber="2" fixed="true">(0,0)
  <label><m>(0,0)</m></label>
</point>
<point stylenumber="2" fixed="true">(3,3)
  <label><m>(3,3)</m></label>
</point>

<point fixed="true" stylenumber="4">(1,-7)
  <label><m>(x_n, x_{n+1}) = (1, -7)</m></label>
</point>

<lineSegment fixed="true" stylenumber="4" endPoints="(1, -7) (0,-7)" />
<lineSegment fixed="true" stylenumber="4" endPoints="(1, -7) (1, 0)" />

</graph>


<p>The equilibria are <m>E=$equilibria </m>.</p>
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
We must solve the equation <m>$equilibria_expression =0</m>.  Factoring out the <m>E</m>, the expression becomes
<me>E(E^2-9)=0.</me>
Continuing factoring, the equation becomes
<me>E(E-3)(E+3)=0.</me>
The equilibria are <m>E=-3,0,3</m>.
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<m>x_1 = f(x_0)= f($x0ex1 ) = $x0ex1 </m>.

<p>We are at an equilibrium, so <m>f</m> does not change the value.  <m>x_1=$x0ex1 </m>, <m>x_2=$x0ex1 </m>, <m>x_3=$x0ex1 </m>.</p>
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
The point with <m>x_0=1</m> is shown on the above graph.  Since the point has coordinates <m>(1,-7)</m>, we see that <m>x_1=-7</m>.

<p>Checking analytically: <m>x_1 = f(x_0)= f(1) = 1^3-8(1) = -7</m>.</p>
</exercise>


</solution>


</problem>